WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.786 --> 00:00:09.109
"Mr. D.! Mr. D.! Mr. D.!" the spectators chanted at the girls' basketball game. There weren't

2
00:00:09.110 --> 00:00:16.547
many people in the bleachers, but they were loud. Mr. D. acknowledged his new fans with

3
00:00:16.548 --> 00:00:22.364
a wave while the hip-hop crew swarmed around him. "Where did you learn to dance

4
00:00:22.365 --> 00:00:32.024
like that?" Javier still couldn't believe that their faculty adviser, who'd never shown much interest in

5
00:00:32.025 --> 00:00:37.674
dancing, had filled in for Pablo. "Come on, guys, the second half of the game is

6
00:00:37.675 --> 00:00:44.408
about to start. Let's get off the court, and I'll explain." Back in the gym office,

7
00:00:44.409 --> 00:00:50.502
the guys fired questions at the teacher. "Whoa! One at a time!" Mr. D. held up

8
00:00:50.503 --> 00:00:58.400
his hands and laughed. "I believe the first question was about where I learned to dance.

9
00:00:58.401 --> 00:01:04.233
Well, I wasn't always an English teacher, you know. I was once a kid who—"

10
00:01:04.234 --> 00:01:10.163
"No, that can't be true!" Will said in mock disbelief. "And I used to do hip-hop."

11
00:01:10.164 --> 00:01:16.321
"That's amazing," Christopher said. Harry just nodded in agreement as Mr. D. continued talking about his

12
00:01:16.322 --> 00:01:20.803
longtime interest in hip-hop. "But why didn't you tell us this before?" Javier asked. "You guys

13
00:01:20.804 --> 00:01:30.384
needed to work things out on your own. But also, when I was 13, I wouldn't

14
00:01:30.385 --> 00:01:35.444
have wanted some teacher trying to be cool and telling me what to do." "If Pablo

15
00:01:35.445 --> 00:01:42.022
doesn't come back, you'll have to join us," Javier joked. "No, this was a onetime

16
00:01:42.023 --> 00:01:49.531
thing." Mr. D. handed his mask to Christopher. *** At the next practice, Pablo showed up

17
00:01:49.532 --> 00:01:54.369
as usual. He'd missed the basketball game because his parents had grounded him that day. They'd

18
00:01:54.370 --> 00:02:01.201
also taken his phone, which explained why he couldn't answer Will's texts. To Javier's surprise, Malcolm

19
00:02:01.202 --> 00:02:11.354
and Marty showed up for practice too. The two of them stayed outside the gym, though,

20
00:02:11.355 --> 00:02:14.683
peeking through the windows. Mr. D. finally covered the windows with brown paper, so they couldn't

21
00:02:14.684 --> 00:02:23.504
spy anymore. "I don't know why they'd want to steal our choreography. We're nowhere near

22
00:02:23.505 --> 00:02:27.329
ready for Best American Talent ," Will complained. The boys were sitting on the floor, taking

23
00:02:27.330 --> 00:02:38.074
a break. "Don't worry. We'll be fine for the audition." Javier took a long drink from

24
00:02:38.075 --> 00:02:44.327
his water bottle and wiped his mouth with the back of his hand. "We just need

25
00:02:44.328 --> 00:02:51.168
more practice." "I'm not sure exactly what our problem is, but we've definitely got one," Christopher

26
00:02:51.169 --> 00:02:56.482
said. Harry raised an eyebrow sharply. Javier started to respond. "We'll be fine if we just—"

27
00:02:56.483 --> 00:03:02.163
"No," Pablo interrupted firmly. "Will and Christopher are right. I have no idea what's wrong

28
00:03:02.164 --> 00:03:05.822
with our dance either. But we're not ready for that audition." Javier suddenly realized that everybody

29
00:03:05.823 --> 00:03:11.061
was looking at him. "Why are you all staring at me? I was too busy dancing

30
00:03:11.062 --> 00:03:20.642
to even notice there was a problem. I don't know what to do . . ."

31
00:03:20.643 --> 00:03:27.967
He paused. "Unless . . . unless . . . what if we asked Mr. D.

32
00:03:27.968 --> 00:03:33.791
to help us?" "Do you think he would?" Will mumbled. "Go ask him, Javier! We'll wait

33
00:03:33.792 --> 00:03:38.122
here," Pablo said. Javier rolled his eyes. "Why me? I just want to dance." "Because

34
00:03:38.123 --> 00:03:43.778
you're good at talking to teachers," said Christopher. Harry nudged Javier with his elbow. "Okay, okay,

35
00:03:43.779 --> 00:03:54.910
I'm going!" Ten minutes later Mr. D. was out on the gym floor, watching them dance.

36
00:03:54.911 --> 00:04:00.090
When they finished, he called them into a huddle. "Well, I'm not sure where to begin

37
00:04:00.091 --> 00:04:07.930
. . ." Mr. D. ran his hands through his hair. "You've got some nice moves

38
00:04:07.931 --> 00:04:21.422
here, but you're not in sync. If everyone's moves are crisp and clean, the whole

39
00:04:21.423 --> 00:04:26.405
dance will look more harmonious. Turn on the music, Will." Mr. D. stepped away from the

40
00:04:26.406 --> 00:04:30.643
huddle and demonstrated a few steps. "Hit those beats precisely. Like this. All right, everybody, let's

41
00:04:30.644 --> 00:04:37.241
try that again." Mr. D. made the crew run through the same moves again and again.

42
00:04:37.242 --> 00:04:40.328
By the end of the afternoon, they were tired of practicing. But Mr. D. was still

43
00:04:40.329 --> 00:04:45.300
full of energy. He seemed very enthusiastic about coaching! *** Every afternoon, Mr. D. worked on

44
00:04:45.301 --> 00:04:50.982
a different aspect of their choreography. As it turned out, he knew a lot about

45
00:04:50.983 --> 00:04:54.384
hip-hop, and he had an eye for detail. "Keep your spacing even!" he shouted at them

46
00:04:54.385 --> 00:04:59.294
one day. "Don't you people ever count?" he roared in exasperation another day. "We've created a

47
00:04:59.295 --> 00:05:10.783
monster," Will said to Javier at the end of that practice. It was right after Mr.

48
00:05:10.784 --> 00:05:15.446
D. had explained the importance of counting—with lots and lots of detail. "Mr. D. was right.

49
00:05:15.447 --> 00:05:24.853
No one wants a teacher telling them how to dance." "Why did he say we should

50
00:05:24.854 --> 00:05:29.931
remember that we're dancing , not just doing tricks?" Pablo said. "He was picking on

51
00:05:29.932 --> 00:05:33.786
me for no good reason." "Maybe we'd be better off without him," Christopher said. "What do

52
00:05:33.787 --> 00:05:42.424
you think?" Nobody said anything for a moment. "I think he's trying to show us that

53
00:05:42.425 --> 00:05:50.757
everything—down to the smallest gesture—has to be perfect." Javier looked directly at Pablo. "The big moves

54
00:05:50.758 --> 00:05:52.860
are really important. But so is everything else. And everybody on this crew has an important

55
00:05:52.861 --> 00:05:58.272
role to play." Harry nodded quickly. "We can take a vote, but I think we're getting

56
00:05:58.273 --> 00:06:01.272
better with Mr. D.," Javier said. The guys decided to keep their coach. *** As

57
00:06:01.273 --> 00:06:06.826
the weeks passed, the crew's dancing continued to improve under Mr. D.'s guidance. The crowd coming

58
00:06:06.827 --> 00:06:13.494
to the girls' basketball games kept growing, and it wasn't just because the team was winning.

59
00:06:13.495 --> 00:06:22.249
Word was getting around that the hip-hop crew was fun to watch. Everyone also knew that

60
00:06:22.250 --> 00:06:30.742
they were auditioning for Best American Talent . On the day before the big audition, the

61
00:06:30.743 --> 00:06:36.557
crew practiced as usual. It was an extra-long practice, but Mr. D. wasn't finished yet. "I've

62
00:06:36.558 --> 00:06:41.461
managed to find some video clips about what it's like when the show comes to

63
00:06:41.462 --> 00:06:44.795
town," said Mr. D. He'd hooked up a computer, so he could project the videos onto

64
00:06:44.796 --> 00:06:48.460
a screen in the gym. "You'll see interviews with performers and samples of the acts. There

65
00:06:48.461 --> 00:06:52.302
are even segments with the judges discussing the acts. You'll get a real sense of what

66
00:06:52.303 --> 00:06:59.541
the audition will be like tomorrow." The five boys watched the videos in silence. At the

67
00:06:59.542 --> 00:07:05.357
end Mr. D. flipped on the lights. "So, what do you think? Are you ready for

68
00:07:05.358 --> 00:07:11.697
tomorrow?" He sounded excited. Javier was almost always optimistic. But today no encouraging words came

69
00:07:11.698 --> 00:07:18.857
out of his mouth. He couldn't even speak. The rest of the crew sat there, looking

70
00:07:18.858 --> 00:07:27.676
just as stunned as he felt. They all knew it—tomorrow was going to be a disaster.

